# Copy to .env in this directory. Expo reads it from the app root and inlines
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* values into the JavaScript bundle at build time.
#
# Nothing secret belongs here. This file's values ship inside the APK, which is
# trivially unpacked (invariant 12). An origin is fine; a token is not.

# Absolute origin of the Fastify API. There is no same-origin server to fall
# back to on a handset, so a relative /sync resolves to nothing.
#
# Without it the app still opens and still records everything — the projection
# it renders is a local SQLite file and needs no server. What it will not do is
# sync: the loop is never started, and the chip reads "Not set up" in the colour
# kept for things waiting cannot fix. That distinction is the point. A device
# that quietly queued all morning, reporting the ordinary offline story, would
# hide the problem until somebody thought to check.
#
# The one case where it is fatal is a device with nobody signed in, because
# signing in is a server round trip and there is no offline answer to give.
#
#   Android emulator  → the host machine is 10.0.2.2, never localhost
#   Physical handset  → your machine's LAN address, e.g. 192.168.1.20
#
# The API listens on 3001 by default.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:3001
